@startuml Transcript Management Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title SABER Transcript Management Flow\nWebSocket-Based Bidirectional Synchronization

' ============================================================================
' PARTICIPANTS
' ============================================================================

box "Client Side (Inspect AI)" #LightBlue
    participant "Agent\n(generate loop)" as Agent
    participant "WebSocketTranscript\nSyncingModelWrapper" as Wrapper
    participant "TranscriptSync\nOperations" as ClientSync
    participant "WebSocketEvent\nProcessor" as EventProc
    participant "WebSocketConnection\nManager" as ConnMgr
end box

box "Network" #LightGray
    participant "WebSocket\nConnection" as WS
end box

box "Server Side" #LightGreen
    participant "WebSocket\nEndpoint" as WSEndpoint
    participant "WebSocketMessage\nRouter" as Router
    participant "TranscriptCoordinator" as Coordinator
    participant "TranscriptState\nMachine" as StateMachine
    participant "ConnectionManager" as ServerConn
    participant "Episode\n(context store)" as Episode
end box

' ============================================================================
' LEGEND - STATE MACHINE
' ============================================================================

note over StateMachine #Yellow
**Transcript State Machine**
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
States:
• WAITING_FOR_USER
• WAITING_FOR_ASSISTANT
• WAITING_FOR_TOOLS

Transitions:
• USER → ASSISTANT (valid)
• ASSISTANT → TOOLS (if tool_calls)
• ASSISTANT → USER (no tool_calls)
• TOOLS → USER (all responded)

Events sent:
• is_waiting_on_user
• is_waiting_on_assistant
• is_waiting_on_tools
end note

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 1: CONNECTION ESTABLISHMENT
' ============================================================================

== Phase 1: WebSocket Connection Establishment ==

Agent -> Wrapper: generate(input, tools)
note right: First generate() call
activate Wrapper

Wrapper -> ConnMgr: ensure_connected()
activate ConnMgr

ConnMgr -> WS: WebSocket connect\n/api/v1/episodes/{episode_id}/ws
activate WS

WS -> WSEndpoint: Accept connection
activate WSEndpoint

WSEndpoint -> ServerConn: connect(episode_id, websocket)
ServerConn -> ServerConn: Register connection

WSEndpoint -> Coordinator: get_initial_state_event(episode_id)
Coordinator -> StateMachine: get_state(episode)
StateMachine -> Episode: Get CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT
Episode --> StateMachine: transcript[]
StateMachine --> Coordinator: TranscriptState.WAITING_FOR_ASSISTANT
Coordinator --> WSEndpoint: StateEventMessage

WSEndpoint --> WS: {"type": "connected", ...}
WSEndpoint --> WS: {"type": "is_waiting_on_assistant",\n  "data": {"state": "WAITING_FOR_ASSISTANT", "version": 0}}

WS --> ConnMgr: Connected + Initial State
ConnMgr -> EventProc: start_listener(websocket)
note right: Background task\nlistens for events
EventProc --> ConnMgr: listener_task
ConnMgr --> Wrapper: ✓ Connected
deactivate ConnMgr
deactivate WSEndpoint

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 2: INITIAL TRANSCRIPT PULL
' ============================================================================

== Phase 2: Initial Transcript Sync (Pull) ==

Wrapper -> EventProc: wait_for_state_event_with_retry()
EventProc -> EventProc: Check event_queue
note right: Initial state event\nalready in queue
EventProc --> Wrapper: event_received = True

Wrapper -> ClientSync: request_sync(websocket)
activate ClientSync

ClientSync -> WS: {"type": "sync_request",\n  "data": {"since_version": 0, "client_checksum": null}}
WS -> Router: route(data, websocket, episode_id)
Router -> Router: SyncRequestHandler.handle()

Router -> Coordinator: sync(TranscriptSyncRequest)
activate Coordinator

Coordinator -> Episode: Get CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT
Episode --> Coordinator: transcript[]

Coordinator -> Coordinator: Compute checksum\nDetermine sync_mode

note right of Coordinator #Pink
**Sync Mode Decision:**
• NO_CHANGE: client up-to-date
• DELTA: client behind, checksum valid
• FULL: checksum mismatch (rewrite)
end note

Coordinator --> Router: TranscriptSyncResponse\n(sync_mode=FULL, full_transcript=[...])
deactivate Coordinator

Router --> WS: {"type": "sync_response",\n  "data": {"sync_mode": "full", "full_transcript": [...]}}

WS --> ClientSync: sync_response
ClientSync -> ClientSync: apply_sync_response()
note right: Update local_messages\nlocal_version\nlocal_checksum
ClientSync --> Wrapper: Updated messages
deactivate ClientSync

Wrapper --> Agent: input = [system, user, ...]
note right: Agent now has\nserver transcript

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 3: AGENT GENERATES RESPONSE
' ============================================================================

== Phase 3: Agent Generates & Pushes Response ==

Agent -> Agent: LLM generates response
Agent --> Wrapper: ModelOutput(message)

Wrapper -> ClientSync: push_message_with_retry(websocket, message)
activate ClientSync

ClientSync -> WS: {"type": "push_message",\n  "data": {"message": {...}, "since_version": 1}}

WS -> Router: route(data, websocket, episode_id)
Router -> Router: PushMessageHandler.handle()

Router -> Coordinator: sync(TranscriptSyncRequest\n  with messages_to_push)
activate Coordinator

Coordinator -> Coordinator: _is_duplicate_push()?
note right: Idempotency check\nfor client retries

Coordinator -> Coordinator: _push_messages(episode, messages)

Coordinator -> Episode: Update CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT
Coordinator -> Episode: Update TRANSCRIPT_VERSION++

Coordinator -> StateMachine: get_state(episode)
note right: Analyze new transcript\nfor state transition
StateMachine --> Coordinator: New state

alt Has tool_calls
    StateMachine --> Coordinator: WAITING_FOR_TOOLS
else No tool_calls
    StateMachine --> Coordinator: WAITING_FOR_USER
end

Coordinator -> Episode: Update CURRENT_TRANSCRIPT_STATE

Coordinator -> ServerConn: broadcast_to_episode(StateEventMessage)
note right: Notify all connected\nclients of state change

Coordinator --> Router: TranscriptSyncResponse
deactivate Coordinator

Router --> WS: {"type": "push_ack",\n  "data": {"version": 2, "checksum": "..."}}

WS --> ClientSync: push_ack
ClientSync -> ClientSync: Update local state
ClientSync --> Wrapper: True (success)
deactivate ClientSync

Wrapper --> Agent: output
deactivate Wrapper

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 4: TOOL EXECUTION FLOW
' ============================================================================

== Phase 4: Tool Execution & Results Push ==

note over Agent #LightYellow
Agent executes tools locally
(Inspect AI handles tool execution)
Agent receives tool results
end note

Agent -> Wrapper: generate(input + tool_results, tools)
activate Wrapper

Wrapper -> ClientSync: push_tool_results_if_needed()
activate ClientSync

note right of ClientSync
Compare local_messages count
with input length to detect
new tool result messages
end note

loop For each tool result message
    ClientSync -> WS: {"type": "push_message",\n  "data": {"message": {"role": "tool", ...}}}
    WS -> Router: PushMessageHandler
    Router -> Coordinator: _push_messages()
    Coordinator -> Episode: Append to CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT
    Coordinator -> StateMachine: get_state()

    alt All tool_calls responded
        StateMachine --> Coordinator: WAITING_FOR_USER
    else Still pending tool_calls
        StateMachine --> Coordinator: WAITING_FOR_TOOLS
    end

    Coordinator -> ServerConn: broadcast_to_episode()
    Router --> WS: push_ack
    WS --> ClientSync: ✓
end

ClientSync --> Wrapper: True
deactivate ClientSync

note right: Agent continues\ngeneration loop

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 5: RED TEAM INJECTION (Cross-Episode)
' ============================================================================

== Phase 5: Red Team Injection (Optional) ==

box "Red Team" #LightCoral
    participant "Red Team\nDaemon" as RedDaemon
end box

RedDaemon -> WSEndpoint: connect(red_episode_id)
note over RedDaemon #Pink
Red team connects with its own
episode_id but can target blue
end note

RedDaemon -> WS: {"type": "push_message",\n  "data": {\n    "target_episode_id": "blue_episode",\n    "message": {"role": "user", "content": "..."},\n    "strategy": "append"\n  }}

WS -> Router: PushMessageHandler (cross-episode)
Router -> Router: is_cross_episode = True

Router -> Coordinator: sync(TranscriptSyncRequest)
activate Coordinator

Coordinator -> Episode: Get blue episode
Coordinator -> Coordinator: _push_messages()
note right: Inject into blue\nteam's transcript

Coordinator -> StateMachine: get_state()
StateMachine --> Coordinator: WAITING_FOR_ASSISTANT

Coordinator -> Episode: Increment MODIFICATION_COUNT

Coordinator -> ServerConn: broadcast_to_episode(\n  target=blue_episode_id,\n  StateEventMessage)
note right #Pink: Blue agent\nreceives injection\nnotification

Coordinator --> Router: TranscriptSyncResponse
deactivate Coordinator

Router --> WS: push_ack (to red team)

' Blue agent receives notification
ServerConn --> WS: {"type": "is_waiting_on_assistant",\n  "data": {"injected_by": "red_episode"}}

note over Wrapper #Yellow
Event queued in EventProcessor
Blue agent will sync on next generate()
end note

WS --> EventProc: State event received
EventProc -> EventProc: Queue event

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 6: BLUE AGENT PROCESSES INJECTION
' ============================================================================

== Phase 6: Blue Agent Processes Injection ==

Agent -> Wrapper: generate() [next iteration]
activate Wrapper

Wrapper -> EventProc: wait_for_state_event_with_retry()
EventProc --> Wrapper: event_received = True\n(injection notification)

Wrapper -> ClientSync: request_sync(websocket)
ClientSync -> WS: sync_request

WS -> Coordinator: sync()
Coordinator -> Coordinator: Detect checksum mismatch\n(transcript was modified)

Coordinator --> WS: {"type": "sync_response",\n  "data": {"sync_mode": "full", ...}}
note right #Pink
FULL sync because
checksum doesn't match
(injection modified transcript)
end note

WS --> ClientSync: sync_response
ClientSync -> ClientSync: apply_sync_response()\nReplace entire local transcript
ClientSync --> Wrapper: Updated messages

Wrapper --> Agent: input = [system, user, ..., injected_message]
deactivate Wrapper

note over Agent
Agent now sees the
injected message and
continues processing
end note

' ============================================================================
' PHASE 7: RESTART OPERATION
' ============================================================================

== Phase 7: Restart Operation (Optional) ==

note over RedDaemon #LightCoral
Red team can reset blue transcript
to INITIAL_TRANSCRIPT and inject
a new message (conversation reset)
end note

RedDaemon -> WS: {"type": "push_message",\n  "data": {\n    "target_episode_id": "blue_episode",\n    "strategy": "restart",\n    "message": {"role": "user", "content": "New prompt"}\n  }}

WS -> Coordinator: sync() with operation=restart
activate Coordinator

Coordinator -> Episode: Get INITIAL_TRANSCRIPT
note right: Captured after first\ncomplete assistant turn

Coordinator -> Coordinator: _push_messages(\n  operation=restart)

note right of Coordinator #Yellow
**Restart Logic:**
1. Get INITIAL_TRANSCRIPT (safe checkpoint)
2. Replace CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT with:
   INITIAL_TRANSCRIPT + new_message
3. Increment version
end note

Coordinator -> Episode: Update CLIENT_TRANSCRIPT
Coordinator -> ServerConn: broadcast(sync_mode=FULL)
Coordinator --> WS: push_ack
deactivate Coordinator

note over Wrapper
Blue agent receives FULL sync
with reset transcript on next
generate() call
end note

' ============================================================================
' CLEANUP
' ============================================================================

== Phase 8: Cleanup ==

Agent -> Wrapper: cleanup()
activate Wrapper

Wrapper -> EventProc: stop_listener()
EventProc -> EventProc: Cancel listener_task

Wrapper -> ConnMgr: cleanup()
ConnMgr -> WS: close()
WS -> WSEndpoint: Disconnect
WSEndpoint -> ServerConn: disconnect(episode_id, websocket)
ServerConn -> ServerConn: Remove from active_connections

WS --> ConnMgr: Closed
Wrapper --> Agent: ✓ Cleanup complete
deactivate Wrapper

@enduml
